messages.text:
The second, focused #6296 review has started with a fresh reviewer (`3ab6aee5`). I gave it the six prior findings and their counterexamples verbatim, because the earlier report directory was empty after closing. The corrected patch applies cleanly to `e638bb9` in a scratch worktree.

The review is read-only and does four things:
- confirms each of the six findings is actually fixed, not just moved;
- reads the six new regression tests to check that each would really fail without its fix;
- sorts each limitation the implementer documented as either an acceptable existing limit, where the answer stays incomplete, or a new way to get a confident wrong answer;
- looks for defects the corrections introduced, including in schema migration 0202.

I'll send the verdict to the CI-monitor session when it's back.

The third #6296 review is running, with reviewer `b2611f0f`. The new patch applies cleanly to `af0aa979`. The reviewer is briefed on:
- the three blocking defects from last round (B1 same-name twin, B2 inheritance, B3 ignored SDK-glob sources) with their counterexamples;
- the earlier findings, as regression checks;
- the CI-monitor session's eight areas, including member and overload identity by physical declaration, the qualified, `global::` and alias tiers, and the external fallback;
- whether the six new tests really discriminate.

The previous reviewers couldn't write to their report directories, so this one returns everything in its handback, and I'll save that verbatim beside the inputs.
